tasks.spec:
You are replacing two discredited structural checkers with a real gate, to a supervising reviewer's specification. BOUNDARY: write only inside your task directory; never call an API, never git commit. You own exactly four output files: ./check_candidate_gate.py, ./check_suppression_delta.py, ./redproof_run.py, ./report.md.

WHY THE OLD ONES FAILED. ./source/check_v57_fixes.py passed a change as having 'evidence for all four fixes' while two did not work: it greps prompts globally for words, so the words can sit on an unreachable node; it never asserts edges reach the clarification node; it cannot see internal prompt contradictions. ./source/check_suppression_wiring.py compares EVERY node against a baseline, so any unrelated legitimate change makes it fail, which buried the suppression signal. Read both, and the reviewer's requirements in ./source/CODEX-RULINGS.txt section R1.4 plus the eight-requirement list referenced there.

BUILD check_candidate_gate.py, asserting on graph JSON topology, never on word presence alone:
(1) exact mixed-intent topology: every offer node (n_offer, n_offer_2, n_offer_3, n_offer_near) has an edge to n_which_intent, and n_which_intent's outgoing edges reach only clarification-legitimate targets (the gates via a later selection, n_negotiate, e_declined, e_timeout), never a book node directly;
(2) no edge from n_which_intent or any offer node reaches n_book_1 or n_book_2 directly, and the only inbound to each book node is its verify node;
(3) outside-hours: n_search carries a day_part == outside route ordered BEFORE every slot-count offer route, targeting n_miss_time, and n_miss_time reaches no offer or book node;
(4) temporal guidance: extraction descriptions contain the qualified-week canon ('tuesday next week' normalization, 'monday next week' vague-week mapping) and do NOT contain the stripping instruction 'must become tuesday';
(5) confirmation monopoly: n_confirm is the only node whose prompt may assert an appointment exists, and e_booked's text contains no second booking claim;
(6) two-slot visibility on every offer node;
(7) suppression isolation via check_suppression_delta.py, see below;
(8) a scenario-inventory guard: given the scenarios file path as an optional argument, verify at least 30 scenarios and that only named assertion fields differ from a recorded manifest of retired fields.

BUILD check_suppression_delta.py: a declared-delta comparator. It takes --graph, --baseline and an explicit --expect-changed list of node ids; it verifies the suppression subgraph invariants (both opt-out exits reachable only through their suppression webhook, correct endpoint path, exact three-field body, retryAttempts 0, no patient-facing claim that the opt-out persisted) AND that nodes outside the expected-changed list are structurally identical to the baseline. Unrelated legitimate changes named in --expect-changed no longer poison the comparison.

BUILD redproof_run.py: the proof that the gate is a gate. It loads source/v57_graph.json, applies AT LEAST EIGHT distinct in-memory mutations, one at a time: remove an offer-to-clarification edge; rewire n_which_intent straight to n_book_1; delete the day_part outside route; reorder it after the offer routes; reinsert the stripping instruction text into an extraction description; add a second booking claim to e_booked's text; give an offer prompt a third slot variable; bypass a suppression node with a direct edge to e_stop. For each mutation, run the relevant checker in-process and FAIL LOUDLY if the checker passes the mutated graph. Also run both checkers on the UNMUTATED graph with a correct --expect-changed list and fail if they do not pass. Print exactly one line 'mutations_caught=N' with the count. Exit 0 only if all mutations were caught and the clean pass succeeded.

Every checker prints WHY it fails, names node ids and the exact broken invariant, and states in its header that it is a structural gate whose pass never substitutes for the live behavioral suite.

OUTPUT CONTRACT for ./report.md: '# Candidate Gate' then '## Summary' (max 3 bullets), '## Invariants Enforced' numbered table mapping each to the reviewer requirement it satisfies, '## Mutations Proven Caught' table, '## What This Still Cannot Prove', '## Assumptions'. Under 700 words.
